---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/base-layout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Documenter"
  description="Documenter processes every file in your browser. There is no upload and no server that sees your documents. Here is exactly how that works."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="container section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        Documenter is built around one promise: <strong>your files never leave your device.</strong>
        This page explains, plainly, what that means and how you can verify it.
      </p>

      <h2>Everything happens in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose a photo, signature or PDF, the file is read and processed by code running
        inside your own browser tab — using the same technologies a web page uses to show an image.
        The resizing, compression and PDF building all run on your device's processor. The result is
        offered back to you as a download.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is <strong>no upload step</strong>. Your document is never sent to Documenter or to any
        other server, because there is no server involved in processing it.
      </p>

      <h2>You can check this yourself</h2>
      <p>
        Open your browser's developer tools and look at the Network tab while you convert a file. You
        will see that no request carries your file's contents anywhere. This is the difference
        between Documenter and most online converters, which upload your file to a server you cannot
        see.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do and don't collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not receive, store, or have any access to the documents you process.</li>
        <li>We do not require an account, and we do not ask for your name or email to use the tools.</li>
        <li>
          The site is static. If analytics or advertising are added later, they will be described
          here before they go live, and they will never have access to your files.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Files you download</h2>
      <p>
        Converted files are created in your browser and saved by you to your own device. Documenter
        keeps no copy because it never had one.
      </p>

      <p>
        Questions about privacy? See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
